[2] Add Product Tab
---------
I am building a pricelist app using Jetpack Compose. So far, there is already a login screen, the app title bar (with username info) and some skeleton code for varios tabs in the main screen. It's also using SQLite and Room to persist data. 
Let's setup the Add Tab in the MainScreen.
Let's focus on the UI first.
Please add the following controls:
1. Tab's Title Area 
The title is "Add Product"  
The entire form can be quite long vertically. 
If the user starts scrolling down, start collapsing the app title bar as the user starts scrolling down. The app's title bar shall collapse completely if the user scrolls down a lot. Similarly, when the user starts scolling up, start revealing back the app title bar.  
2. Category Dropdown control that is searchable using fuzzy search.   
To the right of the Category dropdown, add a plus button for the user to create a new Category. When the user clicks the + button for Category, show a popup form to let the user enter a new category. The popup form shall contain a "Category Name" textbox and 2 buttons: Add and Cancel.
For now, clicking the buttons do nothing.
##When the user clicks Add, please validate against the the local SQLite if the Category already exists. 
3. Product textbox - single line textbox in the sense that user cannot add newline character. If the user types a lot of text, the textbox expands vertically to show the entire text without needing to tackle the cursor. 
4. Description textbox - multiline textbox that allows user to type a newline character. Can we show single line first, then if the user types many text, expand vertically to show all contents.
5. Supplier Dropdown
To the right of the Supplier dropdown, add a plus button for the user to create a new Supplier. When the user clicks the + button for Category, show a popup form to let the user enter a new category. The popup form shall contain a "Supplier Name" textbox and 2 buttons: Add and Cancel.
For now, clicking the buttons does nothing.


5. A button with title "Add Product Variant"
Clicking the "Add Product Variant" button adds a group form with the following controls:
a. Variant Name textbox
Also the same single line textbox behaviour as Product textbox
b. Supplier Price Numeric textbox, 2 decimal places
c. Unit
d. Selling Price Numeric textbox, 2 decimal places
e. A button with title "Add Custom Price"
Clicking the button will append another group form at the bottom of the current Variant form with the following controls:
- Customer Dropdown
To the right of the Supplier dropdown, add a plus button for the user to create a new Customer. When the user clicks the + button for Category, show a popup form to let the user enter a new category. The popup form shall contain a "Customer Name" textbox and 2 buttons: Add and Cancel.
For now, clicking the buttons does nothing.
- Price numeric textbox, 2 decimal places

[3] Initial DB for Products
Now that you have created the UI, let's setup the actual Save function for the Add-Product Tab.
1. Please add a Clear Button and a Save Button at the bottom of the page. The Clear Button will be on the left, while the Save button will be on the right.
2. Clicking the Save button saves the product to the SQLite Database.
3. Same for the Supplier Dialog and Customer Dialog: If the user clicks OK after filling up the Supplier Name, do a validation that the Supplier/Customer Name is not empty. Also ensure that there is not existing supplier or customer exists in the database with the same name. Popup a toast notification to show the error. If everything is OK, go ahead and save it to the database.
4. Since the database is now wired up, during the app's initial load (e.g. after logging in), please load the customer and supplier list from the database, then save it to either the parent navigation tab control's view model or store it in a global viewmodel. Later on, other tabs will also need the customer and supplier list, so I plan to share the list across different tabs.
The fuzzy search for Customer and Supplier Name must now work/be testable.
Going back to #3 above, if a new supplier or customer is added to the database, please update the viewmodel to add the new customer or supplier. Show a toast notification also that Save was successful, just to inform the user.
5. I want to discuss how the customer or supplier dialog works after being wired up to the database.
Right now, when the dropdown is clicked, you are popping up a new dialog.
The dialog contains a textbox for fuzzy search input.
Below it I presume is a place for listing the fuzzy search result.
This is my desired behavior:
- When the dialog is shown, set the focus on the fuzzy search textbox such that they on screen keyboard will be activated already, ready for the user to type. 
For the search result, if the fuzzy search textbox is still empty, show the last 5 customers or suppliers added into the database. I assume the user has a high likelihood to choose from the last few newly added customers/suppliers.
- When the user starts typing in the fuzzy search textbox, you can wait for 500ms until the user stops typing then do the actual fuzzy search (similar to the debounce function in underscore JS)
- If there is no search result on what the user typed, dynamically display a link or button with title 'add "__" to the Database?'. Clicking the button or link shall save the customer or supplier to the database, then close the dialog. The customer or supplier dropdown in the Add Product form shall have the value of the newly added customer or supplier.

6. Other UI requests for the tab navigation control: For the bottom navigation controls, right now the highlight for the currently selected tab is a very faint bluish color. Can you make it more obvious and give a bolder highlight color?

7. Database Schema: I am listing a suggested schema below, including updates to the past DB schema you already created. I basically renamed the tables/column to not use camel-case, instead use all lower case and underscores.

For the id columns, I also want to use ulid instead of a full blown guid to conserve a bit of storage space, and I like the fact the ulid's first few characters is just the current date.

The tables may have extra columns that it not currently present in the Add Product Tab UI. It's OK, we'll get to those fields next time in other tabs. For now, you can create the field first.

[users]
- id (guid)
- user_name (text)
- last_login_date
- is_deleted

[categories]
- id (ulid)
- name (text)
- description

[suppliers]
- id (ulid)
- name
- address
- contact_num (text)
- notes

[customers]
- id (ulid)
- name
- address
- contact_num (text)
- notes

[product]
- id (ulid)
- name
- description
- cat_id
- supplier_id

[supplier_price_hist]
- id (ulid)
- user_id
- date
- variant_id

[customer_price_hist]
- id (ulid)
- user_id
- date
- variant_id
- customer_id
- is_deleted
- is_default_price

